College Management System - ER Diagram Assignment

Objective

Design an Entity-Relationship (ER) diagram for a College Management System.

Entities

Your diagram must include:

Student

Course

Faculty

Department

Required Relationships and Cardinalities

Relationship

Cardinality

Department has Students

One-to-Many (1)

Faculty handles Courses

One-to-Many (1)

Student enrolls in Course

Many-to-Many (M)

Suggested attributes

You may use these attributes:

Student: StudentID (PK), StudentName, Email

Course: CourseID (PK), CourseName, Credits

Faculty: FacultyID (PK), FacultyName

Department: DepartmentID (PK), DepartmentName

For the M relationship, you may introduce an associative entity such as Enrollment with StudentID and CourseID as foreign keys.

About 1:1

The question asks that one-to-one, one-to-many, and many-to-many relationships be mentioned clearly. The required college relationships include 1 and M, but no 1:1 relationship is specified.

Therefore, do not force a 1:1 label onto a required relationship. If your instructor specifically requires a 1:1 example, add a justified extra entity/relationship and label it separately.

Submission Format

Create the final diagram as:

ER_Diagram.png

Place the file in the root of your GitHub repository.

How to Submit

Clone/open your assigned repository.

Create ER_Diagram.png.

Make sure the diagram is readable.

Commit and push the file.

Check the Actions tab.

A successful submission should show all automated tests passing.

Grading

The automated checker verifies:

ER_Diagram.png exists.

The file is a valid PNG.

The image is not empty or extremely small.

The diagram is large enough to be reasonably readable.

Content/cardinality correctness is also part of the instructor's manual evaluation.
